  "generated_text": "1. **Identify the length of AD:**\n   From the given information, we know that $AD = 37$ units.\n\n2. **Identify the length of CD:**\n   Similarly, we know that $CD = 19$ units.\n\n3. **Calculate the length of AC:**\n   Since $AC = AD - CD$, we have:\n   \\[\n   AC = 37 - 19 = 18 \\text{ units}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Apply the Pythagorean Theorem in triangle ABC:**\n   In triangle ABC, we have:\n   \\[\n   BC^2 = AB^2 - AC^2\n   \\]\n   Substituting the known values:\n   \\[\n   BC^2 = 37^2 - 18^2\n   \\]\n   Calculating the squares:\n   \\[\n   BC^2 = 1369 - 324 = 1045\n   \\]\n   Taking the square root:\n   \\[\n   BC = \\sqrt{1045}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the length of segment BC is $\\boxed{\\sqrt{1045}}$ units.",
